{
 "_doc": [
  "Per-chassis orientation corrections, applied by export-roster.py.",
  "",
  "MEASURED, not guessed. Forward comes from the vector between the CHEST and",
  "the SPINE of the robot pose: chest is the front of a torso and spine is the",
  "back, so it points forward whatever the model is called and whatever its",
  "parts are labelled. An earlier attempt used a left/right limb pair, which",
  "was circular \u2014 it assumes which limb is which, so it agreed with itself on",
  "all 28 and told us nothing.",
  "",
  "`turn` spends the rotation ACROSS the fold, so the vehicle keeps the facing",
  "it has and only the robot end moves. That is right here because the reading",
  "is about the robot pose."
 ],
